  "expected_answer": "functional skipped (signed-in check), context pass, load pass, accessibility FAIL: brand colour #FFE680 on white has a contrast of about 1.3:1, needs 4.5:1; responsiveness not run (pending). alpha_app is now reverted and a fix task was filed.",
  "final_text": "The tests didn't pass. The accessibility check failed because the brand colour is too pale to read on white. As a result alpha_app has been set to `reverted`, and the run stopped before reaching the last lane.\n\n| Lane | Result | Detail |\n|---|---|---|\n| Functional | Skipped (not a pass) | 2 of 3 checks passed. `chat.turn` didn't run because it needs someone signed in. |\n| Context | **Pass** | 1 of 1 |\n| Load | **Pass** | 1 of 1 |\n| Accessibility | **Fail** | `brand.contrast` failed, and `authenticated.surface` was skipped because it also needs someone signed in. |\n| Responsiveness | Did not run | The run stops at the first failure, so this was reset to `pending`. |\n\n**Why it failed:** alpha_app's brand colour is `#FFE680`, a light yellow, set at `state/application/alpha_app/application.json:239`. On a white background it has a contrast of 1.2:1. Buttons and links need at least 4.5:1 to meet the standard accessibility guideline (WCAG AA), so text in that colour would be very hard to read. This is a problem with the app's branding, not with the tests. Task **mold_v1-009** was filed for it automatically. Full report: `molds/mold_v1/testing/accessibility/reports/alpha_app-2026-10-09T140934Z.md`.\n\nThe whole run took about 2 seconds. The report says these lanes are a rehearsal stand-in checked against a fake deployment, not the full real-world measurements.\n\n**Next steps:**\n1. **Choose a darker brand colour.** Keeping the yellow would need a dark shade; a deep gold or brown would pass, for example. Tell me the colour you want, or ask me to suggest a few that pass, and I'll update it and rerun all five lanes.\n2. **Fill the skipped checks (optional).** Three checks need someone who can sign in to alpha_app. That person would get a one-time code by email, which I'll only request if you say so and tell me whose email address to use. Until then, Functional and Accessibility can at best show \"skipped\", never \"pass\".",
